> ### **Glocalization in Architecture**
> The study of second-wave coffee shops like Starbucks unveils how global brands adapt to local cultures. By incorporating local architectural elements into their standardized formats, these coffee shops create a unique cultural blend that resonates with local communities while maintaining global brand identity. This approach, known as "glocalization," highlights the interplay between global business strategies and local cultural expressions [77253].
